---
import Section from "./Section.astro";
import ScreenshotPlaceholder from "./ScreenshotPlaceholder.astro";

const steps = [
  {
    at: "0s",
    title: "Find the animal",
    body: "Search by name, microchip, band, case number or enclosure. Or open the enclosure you are standing in front of and pick from who lives there.",
  },
  {
    at: "8s",
    title: "Tap a category",
    body: "Your organization's categories, not ours. Feeding, behaviour, treatment, enrichment - whatever your team already says out loud.",
  },
  {
    at: "15s",
    title: "Write the sentence, take the photo",
    body: "One line is a complete record. The photo comes straight from the camera. What you observed and when you observed it are stored separately from when you typed it.",
  },
  {
    at: "30s",
    title: "Save",
    body: "It is in the permanent record, attributed to you, searchable, and visible to whoever walks in next. Nobody types it a second time.",
  },
];
---

<Section
  id="how"
  eyebrow="How it works"
  title="One capture, at the enclosure, in about thirty seconds."
  lead="ARK is built around a single loop. Every other feature hangs off it, and nothing is allowed to make it slower."
>
  <ol
    class="mt-14 grid gap-px overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border bg-border sm:grid-cols-2"
  >
    {
      steps.map((step) => (
        <li class="reveal bg-card p-7 sm:p-8">
          <p class="eyebrow" aria-hidden="true">
            {step.at}
          </p>
          <h3 class="mt-3 text-xl">{step.title}</h3>
          <p class="mt-2.5 text-muted-foreground">{step.body}</p>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ol>

  <div
    class="reveal mt-8 grid items-center gap-10 rounded-2xl border border-border bg-muted/60 p-7 sm:p-10 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_auto] lg:gap-14"
  >
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">When the network is not there</p>
      <h3 class="mt-3 text-2xl text-balance">Capture does not wait for a connection.</h3>
      <div class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-muted-foreground">
        <p>
          We are not going to tell you that dead spots at enclosures are this sector's great
          unsolved problem, because we could not find anyone saying so. What facilities do report is
          the ordinary kind of outage: the site's internet goes down for an afternoon and work
          carries on regardless.
        </p>
        <p>
          So ARK treats the network as optional rather than assumed. A note, a photo, a weight or a
          feeding is written on the device and queued. When a connection returns it syncs, and
          because every capture carries an id the device generated, a retry is acknowledged as the
          entry you already made rather than filed as a second one.
        </p>
        <p class="text-foreground">
          Offline capture is on every plan, including Starter. It is insurance, and insurance you
          only get on the expensive tier is not insurance.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <ScreenshotPlaceholder
      class="justify-self-center lg:justify-self-end"
      label="Captured offline, waiting to sync"
      shot="An animal profile in airplane mode with a just-saved log carrying the pending-sync chip, and the offline indicator visible in the app chrome."
      viewport="390 x 844, light mode, airplane mode on"
      frame="phone"
    />
  </div>
</Section>
